{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>For all this</b> etc. — לבור [to know]. It should have been with holeq, and likewise ירון, both being of the doubled [root] pattern; it is like לברור, from \"her lips speak לברור\" [clearly]. For I have seen the righteous and the wise and their deeds — as in \"he will recognize from his servants\" — are not in their own power but in the hand of Elohim. Also all that they love or hate, they do not know when it will come upon them, nor will they perceive it. Or the meaning of \"before them\" is: before they come to be, it has already been decreed upon them what is decreed."], :book :ecclesiastes, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {0 "The Hebrew repeatedly uses בחול״ם (with holeq); I render it 'holeq' following the grammatical term for short holam. The phrase מפעלי הכפל refers to roots with a doubled middle radical. The verse citation behind \"he will recognize from his servants\" is uncertain; possibly Nehemiah 13:24 or a similar source."}, :source-witnesses [["Wikisource" "https://he.wikisource.org/wiki/%D7%90%D7%91%D7%9F_%D7%A2%D7%96%D7%A8%D7%90_%D7%A2%D7%9C_%D7%A7%D7%94%D7%9C%D7%AA"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:28:36.502573905Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}